# Signup, email verification, login and sessions (ticket 02).
# Works with the VS Code REST Client or JetBrains HTTP Client.
#
# The refresh token travels in an HttpOnly cookie scoped to /v1/auth/refresh. If your client
# doesn't keep Secure cookies over plain http://localhost, copy the sentinel_refresh value from
# the login response's Set-Cookie header into @refreshToken and uncomment the Cookie headers.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = alice@example.com
@password = correct horse battery
@refreshToken = paste-from-set-cookie

### Public keys for verifying access tokens (Applications cache this)
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### 1. Sign up. Always 202, whether or not the email already has an account.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Alice", "lastName": "Liddell", "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. Verify the email. Copy the token from the link in Mailpit (http://localhost:8025),
###    the part after "#token=". Each token works once.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "paste-token-from-email" }

### Ask for a new verification link
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}" }

### 3. Log in. Returns the access token; sets the refresh-token cookie.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 4. Who am I? (Bearer access token, valid 10 minutes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5. Silent refresh. Each refresh token works once and is replaced by a new cookie.
###    Sending an already-used token again revokes every refresh token from that login.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/refresh
# Cookie: sentinel_refresh={{refreshToken}}

### 6. Log out on this device (revokes the refresh token in the cookie)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/refresh
# Cookie: sentinel_refresh={{refreshToken}}

### 7. Log out everywhere (revokes all of the User's refresh tokens)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Change your name (either field may be omitted)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Alice", "lastName": "Liddell" }
